  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc7dMqNk",
      "title": "feat: szkdg",
      "author": "ashitakah",
      "number": 911,
      "body": "CLOSES https://github.com/orgs/ethereum-optimism/projects/154/views/1?reload=1&pane=issue&itemId=187673182&issue=ethereum-optimism%7Coptimism%7C20746\r\n\r\n# SuperZKDisputeGame Specification\r\n\r\nThis PR introduces the `SuperZKDisputeGame` specification, replacing the earlier single-chain ZK dispute game spec with a Superchain-native design that verifies a super root state transition across all chains in the interop set via a single ZK proof.\r\n\r\n## New Documents\r\n\r\n| File | Description |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `specs/fault-proof/super-zk-fault-proof-vm.md` | Defines the Super ZK Fault Proof VM: the off-chain ZK program and the `IZKVerifier` on-chain interface. Replaces `zk-fault-proof-vm.md`. |\r\n| `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/super-zk-dispute-game.md` | Core game spec: CWIA layout, `rootClaim` semantics, `initialize` invariants, OPCM integration, assumptions, and invariants. Replaces `zk-dispute-game.md`. |\r\n| `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/super-zk-game-mechanics.md` | State machine, creation/challenge/prove/resolve lifecycle, and bond distribution. Replaces `game-mechanics.md`. |\r\n| `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/super-zk-interface.md` | `IZKVerifier` Solidity interface spec and verifier upgrade path. Replaces `zk-interface.md`. |\r\n| `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/super-zk-migration.md` | Three migration paths (`SFDG → SuperZKDG` isolated, `SPDG → SuperZKDG` isolated, `SFDG → SuperZKDG` interop set) via `OPCMv2.upgrade()`. |\r\n\r\n## Key Design Changes vs. Previous ZK Game\r\n\r\n- **Super root instead of single-chain output root.**  \r\n  `rootClaim` commits to a `SuperRoot` covering all chains in the interop set. `rootClaimByChainId` extracts the per-chain output root from the preimage.\r\n\r\n- **Unified standalone + interop.**  \r\n  No separate standalone mode, a single-chain deployment is an interop set of size one. The ZK program and contract are identical in both cases.\r\n\r\n- **`ProposalStatus` internal enum.**  \r\n  Decouples the internal lifecycle:\r\n  - `Unchallenged`\r\n  - `Challenged`\r\n  - `UnchallengedAndValidProofProvided`\r\n  - `ChallengedAndValidProofProvided`\r\n\r\n  from the external `GameStatus`:\r\n  - `IN_PROGRESS`\r\n  - `CHALLENGER_WINS`\r\n  - `DEFENDER_WINS`\r\n\r\n  consumed by `OptimismPortal` and `AnchorStateRegistry`.\r\n\r\n- **MCP clone architecture.**  \r\n  Game args are passed as CWIA calldata (fixed prefix + variable `extraData`), consistent with `SuperFaultDisputeGame`.\r\n\r\n- **Verifier abstraction.**  \r\n  The game depends on `IZKVerifier` rather than a concrete verifier, allowing proving system upgrades without redeploying the game implementation. Initial release targets Succinct SP1 PLONK.\r\n\r\n- **Three migration paths.**  \r\n  Supports migrations from `SuperFaultDisputeGame` and `SuperPermissionedDisputeGame` to `SuperZKDisputeGame`, all executed through `OPCMv2.upgrade()`.\r\n\r\n## Modified Documents\r\n\r\n- `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/zk-dispute-game.md`\r\n- `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/game-mechanics.md`\r\n- `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/zk-interface.md`\r\n- `specs/fault-proof/zk-fault-proof-vm.md`",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
